        "subtopic": "Ecological Fallacy",
        "source": "Qbank",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "question": "A study finds that countries with higher per capita chocolate consumption have more Nobel laureates, and concludes that chocolate consumption increases individual likelihood of winning a Nobel Prize. This flawed inference from group-level to individual-level data is called?",
