        "correct": 2,
        "explanation": "Ecological fallacy is the error of inferring individual-level relationships from data observed only at the aggregate/group level, exactly as in this example. Selection bias concerns how subjects are chosen into a study, not the level of data analysis. Confounding bias involves a third variable affecting the true relationship, which may or may not also be present but is not the named error here. Recall bias concerns differential memory of exposure. Berkson's bias is a specific hospital-based selection bias, unrelated to aggregate data misinterpretation.",
