        "explanation": "Systematic reviews and meta-analyses that pool multiple high-quality RCTs sit at the top of the evidence hierarchy because they combine and statistically synthesize results from multiple rigorous studies, reducing random error and increasing precision. Case reports and expert opinion sit at the bottom, providing the weakest evidence due to lack of systematic control. Cross-sectional studies provide only a snapshot association without establishing temporality. A single cohort study, while stronger than observational case-control designs, still ranks below a well-conducted synthesis of multiple RCTs.",
