        "explanation": "An effect modifier is a variable that genuinely changes (modifies) the strength or direction of an association between exposure and outcome across its different levels/strata, exactly as age does here for drug effectiveness. A confounder distorts the true crude association without truly altering the actual biological effect. A mediator lies on the causal pathway between exposure and outcome, transmitting the effect rather than modifying it. A collider is influenced by both variables and creates bias if conditioned upon. This scenario represents a genuine biological interaction, not a source of bias.",
