        "explanation": "An independent (unpaired) t-test compares means of a continuous, normally distributed variable between two separate, independent groups, exactly matching this scenario. Chi-square tests are for categorical data comparisons, not continuous means. A paired t-test is used when the same subjects are measured twice (e.g., before and after), not for two independent groups. McNemar's test is used for paired categorical (nominal) data, not continuous data. The Wilcoxon signed-rank test is a non-parametric alternative for paired data, not for comparing two independent groups.",
