        "explanation": "The Mann-Whitney U test is the non-parametric equivalent of the independent t-test, appropriate for ordinal data or non-normally distributed continuous data compared between two independent groups. A paired t-test requires related/matched samples and normal distribution assumptions, neither of which applies here. Chi-square tests categorical frequency data, not ranked ordinal scores between groups in this manner. Pearson correlation requires continuous, normally distributed variables to assess linear association, not group comparison of ordinal data. One-way ANOVA is a parametric test for three or more groups with normally distributed continuous data, not suited to two-group non-normal ordinal comparisons.",
