        "explanation": "A paired t-test is specifically designed for comparing two related/matched measurements taken from the same subjects at two different times, exactly matching before-and-after drug measurements. An independent t-test assumes two separate, unrelated groups of subjects, not repeated measurements on the same individuals. Chi-square tests categorical data comparisons, not continuous paired measurements. One-way ANOVA compares means across three or more independent groups, not two related time points within the same subjects. Pearson correlation measures association strength, not mean difference, and is not the appropriate test for this before-after comparison.",
