        "explanation": "Reliability refers to consistency/reproducibility of measurement, and since the scale consistently gives the same (though incorrect) reading each time, it demonstrates high reliability; however, since it does not measure the true value accurately, it has poor validity (accuracy). Poor reliability and poor validity would apply if readings were both inconsistent and inaccurate, which is not the case here since readings are consistent. High validity would require accurate measurement of the true value, which this scale fails to do. Reliability and validity are each clearly assessable from the description given, contradicting the last option.",
