        "explanation": "As sample size increases, the standard error decreases, which narrows the confidence interval and reflects a more precise estimate of the true population parameter. It does not widen with increasing sample size; that would occur with increasing variability or higher confidence level instead. The interval width does change with sample size, so it does not remain the same. Confidence intervals remain calculable at any reasonable sample size, so it does not become impossible. The interval approaches, but never mathematically reaches, exactly zero width even with a very large sample.",
