        "explanation": "SARS-CoV-2 is primarily transmitted through respiratory droplets and aerosols released when an infected person coughs, sneezes, talks, or breathes, with transmission risk particularly elevated in close contact situations and poorly ventilated indoor environments where aerosol accumulation can occur. It is not primarily transmitted via the fecal-oral route like cholera; while viral RNA has been detected in stool in some cases, this is not established as the primary or significant transmission route for COVID-19, unlike classic fecal-orally transmitted diseases. There is no vector-borne transmission mechanism for SARS-CoV-2; no insect vector is involved in its transmission, unlike diseases such as malaria or dengue. It is not primarily transmitted through blood-to-blood contact like HIV; COVID-19's established primary transmission route is specifically respiratory, not blood-borne. It has no established significant transmission route through contaminated soil; this is not a recognized primary transmission mechanism for this specific respiratory virus.",
