        "explanation": "In ECCE, preserving the posterior capsule allows for in-the-bag PCIOL implantation, but residual equatorial lens epithelial cells can proliferate and migrate across the visual axis, causing Posterior Capsule Opacification (PCO / after-cataract) in up to 20\u201350% of cases. PCO cannot occur in ICCE because the entire posterior capsule is removed. ICCE, however, has much higher rates of retinal detachment, vitreous loss, and cystoid macular edema.",
