        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 15-year-old boy presents with progressive knee pain. X-ray shows a destructive, bone-forming mass in the metaphysis of the distal femur. The periosteum is lifted, forming a 'Codman triangle,' and there is a 'sunburst' pattern of bone growth. What is the diagnosis?",
