        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 25-year-old male presents with new-onset resting tremor, dysarthria, and elevated liver enzymes. A slit-lamp examination of his eyes reveals golden-brown rings encircling the iris (Kayser-Fleischer rings). This disease is caused by an inherited defect in a transporter responsible for incorporating which metal into ceruloplasmin?",
