        "topic": "Renal Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 65-year-old male undergoes a prolonged, complex abdominal surgery complicated by severe hypotension. Three days later, he develops oliguria and rising BUN/Creatinine. Urinalysis reveals 'muddy brown' granular casts. Which segment of the nephron is most susceptible to this specific type of injury?",
