        "exp": "Acute Tubular Necrosis (ATN) is the most common cause of acute kidney injury in the hospital, often triggered by ischemia. The proximal convoluted tubule and the thick ascending limb of the loop of Henle are highly metabolically active and are the most susceptible to ischemic necrosis.",
