        "topic": "Hematology",
        "difficulty": "Harder",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 30-year-old female presents with petechiae, purpura, and epistaxis. Her CBC is completely normal except for a platelet count of 15,000/uL. Bone marrow biopsy shows increased numbers of megakaryocytes. What is the pathogenesis of her condition?",
