        "exp": "Secondary (reactivation) Tuberculosis classically occurs in the apices of the lungs (due to high oxygen tension favoring the obligate aerobe Mycobacterium tuberculosis) and forms caseating granulomas that can cavitate. The bacteria stain acid-fast positive.",
