        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A patient with a large pleural effusion undergoes thoracentesis. The fluid is cloudy, has a high protein content (>3g/dL), and high LDH. According to Light's criteria, this fluid is an exudate. Which of the following conditions is most likely responsible?",
