        "exp": "Cigarette smoke acts as a chemoattractant, drawing neutrophils and macrophages into the alveoli. These inflammatory cells release proteases (specifically elastase) which destroy the alveolar walls, while the smoke simultaneously inhibits the body's anti-proteases.",
