        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 60-year-old female non-smoker presents with a cough and copious amounts of watery sputum (bronchorrhea). Chest X-ray shows an ill-defined infiltrate that mimics lobar pneumonia. Biopsy shows columnar, mucin-producing cells growing continuously along the intact alveolar septa without stromal invasion. What is the diagnosis?",
