        "exp": "Bilateral renal Angiomyolipomas (benign hamartomas of blood vessel, muscle, and fat) are highly characteristic of Tuberous Sclerosis Complex. This autosomal dominant disorder also features cortical tubers, subependymal giant cell astrocytomas, and ash-leaf spots on the skin.",
