        "correct": 0,
        "exp": "Chronic pyelonephritis is caused by recurrent infections, usually due to vesicoureteral reflux or chronic obstruction. It features asymmetric cortical scarring and blunted calyces. The hallmark microscopic finding is 'thyroidization of the kidney'\u2014dilated tubules filled with dense eosinophilic casts that look exactly like thyroid tissue.",
        "book": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease",
        "subtopic": "Tubulointerstitial Diseases",
        "id": "GEN-0296"
