        "difficulty": "Harder",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 40-year-old male with a history of chronic lead exposure presents with gout (Saturnine gout) and hypertension. An ultrasound reveals bilaterally shrunken kidneys. Biopsy shows diffuse interstitial fibrosis and tubular atrophy. Which distinct hereditary condition can mimic these exact clinical and radiological findings in young adults without any toxin exposure?",
