        "correct": 1,
        "exp": "Medullary Cystic Kidney Disease is an autosomal dominant condition characterized by cysts in the medullary collecting ducts. Crucially, it causes severe tubulointerstitial fibrosis, leading to progressive renal failure and distinctly SHRUNKEN kidneys in young adults (unlike ADPKD, which causes massively enlarged kidneys).",
        "book": "Pathoma: Fundamentals of Pathology",
