        "topic": "Renal Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 20-year-old male with a history of Hodgkin Lymphoma presents with sudden-onset massive proteinuria, hypoalbuminemia, and pitting edema. Light microscopy of a renal biopsy is completely normal. Why is this specific renal pathology heavily associated with Hodgkin Lymphoma?",
