        "correct": 0,
        "exp": "Minimal Change Disease is typically idiopathic in children, but when it occurs in adults, it is classically associated with Hodgkin Lymphoma. This is because Hodgkin Lymphoma is characterized by massive cytokine production (by Reed-Sternberg cells), which mediates the podocyte foot process effacement seen in MCD.",
