        "exp": "Liddle syndrome mimics hyperaldosteronism (hypertension, hypokalemia, alkalosis) but is caused by a continuously active ENaC channel in the collecting duct. Because sodium is constantly reabsorbed, blood pressure spikes, suppressing both Renin and Aldosterone to near-zero levels. It is treated with Potassium-sparing diuretics like Amiloride.",
