        "exp": "Dialysis-Associated Amyloidosis is caused by the accumulation of Beta-2 microglobulin. This MHC Class I protein is normally filtered by the kidneys but is NOT filtered well by standard dialysis membranes. Over years, it accumulates and deposits as amyloid, classically causing carpal tunnel syndrome.",
