        "exp": "Urothelial (Transitional cell) carcinoma can occur anywhere along the urothelium (bladder, ureters, renal pelvis). Major risk factors spell 'Pee SAC': Phenacetin (analgesics), Smoking, Aniline dyes, and Cyclophosphamide. Analgesic nephropathy specifically increases the risk of upper tract (renal pelvis) urothelial carcinoma.",
