        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 25-year-old female presents with dysuria, urinary frequency, and suprapubic pain. She has no fever and no flank pain. Urinalysis is positive for leukocyte esterase and nitrites. What is the most common causative organism?",
