        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A patient with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) presents with hematuria and RBC casts. Renal biopsy shows focal necrotizing lesions and crescent formation. Immunofluorescence reveals a 'full house' pattern (deposits of IgG, IgA, IgM, C3, and C1q). This is indicative of severe Lupus Nephritis. Where are these massive immune complexes predominantly depositing to cause this severe proliferative response?",
